{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2174-02-15 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mrs. ___. I’m Dr. ___. You’re here because of abdominal pain, nausea, and vomiting. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2174-02-15 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes… I’ve had this pain in my belly for a couple days. I’ve thrown up twice. And swallowing hurts—like something’s stuck."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2174-02-15 18:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you mentioned chest discomfort and shortness of breath too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2174-02-15 18:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, but I think that’s from the pain. It hurts so much when I try to eat or drink."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2174-02-15 18:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. Given your history of radiation for tracheal cancer, we’re concerned about inflammation or narrowing in your esophagus. We’ll run some tests."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2174-02-15 18:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had this before—radiation esophagitis. But this feels worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2174-02-15 18:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll check for infection too. Being on steroids increases your risk for a yeast infection in the esophagus, called candidiasis. We’re starting fluconazole just in case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2174-02-15 18:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ve taken that before. But what about the pain? I can’t even keep water down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2174-02-15 18:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re giving you Zofran for nausea and will keep you hydrated with IV fluids. We also have a mouthwash with lidocaine and Maalox to numb the pain when you swallow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2174-02-15 18:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. That sounds helpful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2174-02-16 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs are stable. White count is normal, so no sign of bacterial infection. Your sputum test was also normal—just typical mouth bacteria."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2174-02-16 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the flu test?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2174-02-16 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Negative. So it’s not influenza. Your cough and congestion are likely from a mild viral upper respiratory infection, which should improve on its own."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2174-02-16 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. But what about the swallowing issue?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2174-02-16 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re scheduling a barium swallow today to look for any narrowing in your esophagus. Given your history, we’re worried about a stricture from past radiation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2174-02-16 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The barium swallow shows a narrowing in your esophagus, about 3 cm long, right at the level of your aortic arch. A 12-mm tablet couldn’t pass through it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2174-02-16 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh no. Does that mean I can’t eat normally?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2174-02-16 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. But we’re not going to dilate it today because there’s too much inflammation. We’ll reduce the swelling first. We’ll do an endoscopy soon to look more closely and take biopsies."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2174-02-17 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve increased your prednisone to 40 mg daily for a week to help with your arthritis pain, then taper down. I know you felt worse when you were off it last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2174-02-17 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, the pain was terrible. Thank you for restarting it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2174-02-17 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re also switching your Nexium to pantoprazole twice a day. It’s stronger and will help reduce stomach acid, which may be irritating your esophagus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2174-02-17 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And I’m still on the fluconazole?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2174-02-17 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, for 14 days. We’re treating for possible candida, especially since you’re on steroids and antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2174-02-18 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your nausea has improved, and you’re tolerating liquids. Your abdominal pain is much better too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2174-02-18 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I had some broth this morning. Felt okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2174-02-18 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll advance you to soft foods. Your bowel regimen is helping too—no constipation now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2174-02-19 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did the endoscopy this morning. There’s severe inflammation and an ulcer at 20 cm in your esophagus. We also saw a small nodule and took biopsies from both."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2174-02-19 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "An ulcer? Is it from the radiation?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2174-02-19 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most likely. The biopsies will tell us more—whether it’s just inflammation or something else. We couldn’t dilate the stricture today because it was too inflamed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2174-02-19 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When can we try dilation?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2174-02-19 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "In a few months, once the inflammation settles. Your GI doctor will schedule a follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2174-02-19 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the nodule? Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2174-02-19 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s small, and we don’t think it’s cancerous, but the biopsy will confirm. Most likely it’s scar tissue from radiation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2174-02-19 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chest X-ray shows no pneumonia or fluid. The old scarring from radiation is still there, but nothing new."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2174-02-19 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. My cough is better too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2174-02-19 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and your oxygen levels are normal. We’ll keep you on your asthma meds—Advair, Spiriva, and nebulizers as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2174-02-20 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure has been high. We’re keeping you on your usual meds—amlodipine, lisinopril, and metoprolol."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2174-02-20 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It runs high when I’m in pain. Is it better now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2174-02-20 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s coming down. We gave you a dose of Lasix yesterday because we saw some leg swelling—just a little fluid buildup."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2174-02-20 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve taken that at home when my feet swell."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2174-02-20 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll send you home with it to use as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2174-02-21 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing much better. You’re eating, pain is controlled, and your breathing is stable. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2174-02-21 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2174-02-21 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue the fluconazole for 14 days. Take pantoprazole twice daily. And follow the prednisone taper: start at 20 mg, then reduce by 2.5 mg each week until you’re at 5 mg."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2174-02-21 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll need to write that down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2174-02-21 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and stop ranitidine—you don’t need it with pantoprazole. Also stop cetirizine; it may be making you drowsy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2174-02-21 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been so tired. I thought it was the pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2174-02-21 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Partly that, but cetirizine can add to it. We’re also stopping metoclopramide since your nausea is gone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2174-02-21 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the biopsies?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2174-02-21 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get a call from GI in about a week with the results. Please follow up with them and your oncologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2174-02-21 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel much better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2174-02-21 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll arrange home health to help you for a few days. Keep using the lidocaine-Maalox mix for pain before meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2174-02-21 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll call if anything changes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2174-02-21 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Especially if pain returns, or you can’t keep food down. Otherwise, see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2174-02-21 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you so much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2174-02-21 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Get some rest at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2174-02-21 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I plan to."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2174-02-21 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will bring your discharge papers and prescriptions shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2174-02-21 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll be ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2174-02-21 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mrs. ___. We’re glad you’re feeling better."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2174-02-15 17:45:00",
    "admission_end": "2174-02-21 18:26:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mrs. ___ was admitted with abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting, and odynophagia, following a recent hospitalization for respiratory symptoms. She has a complex history including prior tracheal cancer treated with radiation, which likely contributed to esophageal stricture and ulceration. A barium swallow revealed a 3 cm esophageal stricture that prevented passage of a 12-mm tablet, and EGD confirmed severe radiation-related esophagitis with an ulcer and nodule, both biopsied. Due to inflammation, dilation was deferred. She was treated empirically for candidal esophagitis with fluconazole and started on high-dose pantoprazole. Her viral upper respiratory infection resolved with supportive care, and her abdominal symptoms improved with antiemetics and bowel management. Prednisone was adjusted for rheumatoid arthritis flare, and her asthma, heart failure, and hypertension were managed. She was discharged home with services on a prednisone taper, pantoprazole, fluconazole, and follow-up plans for biopsy results and GI reevaluation.",
    "problems": [
      "Stricture and stenosis of esophagus",
      "Ulcer of esophagus without bleeding",
      "Other esophagitis",
      "Late effect of radiation",
      "Acute upper respiratory infections of unspecified site",
      "Chronic obstructive asthma, unspecified",
      "Rheumatoid arthritis",
      "Chronic systolic heart failure",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of breast",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of bronchus and lung",
      "Malignant neoplasm of trachea",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Dysphagia, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
